Point.  We currently let each game server specify the UID range in which 
player accounts get created, so you could end up with a different user 
number on each server.  We're looking at changing it so your UID is 
assigned by the control server so the UIDs could be identical; that 
would allow us to rsync the save directories from all the servers.

The only problem that would create would be in the event that a server 
went down while you had a game in progress: you wouldn't be able to just 
switch to another server to play; you'd have to wait till we could get 
that server's games recovered onto a functional box before you started 
up again.

A better solution is probably to use ntp to sync the server's clocks and 
then order the log entries by the game starting time for Best of 13.

